[
    {
        "content": "<p>The statement of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fin.isAddFreimanIso_Iic#doc\">docs#Fin.isAddFreimanIso_Iic</a> relies on casting natural numbers to <code>Fin (n + 1)</code>. Which is part of our <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Technical.20Debt.20Counters/with/586065756\">#mathlib4 &gt; Technical Debt Counters</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isAddFreimanIso_Iic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hkmn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsAddFreimanIso</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Iic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Iic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What would we like this statement to be instead?</p>\n<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span></p>",
        "id": 586078796,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776415995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well <code>k &lt; n + 1</code> is derivable from the assumptions, right</p>",
        "id": 586093306,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776420242
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Using Fin.ofNat here should also work</p>",
        "id": 586094170,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1776420508
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another option is to have <code>k</code> be a term of <code>Fin (n+1)</code> to start with.</p>",
        "id": 586108308,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776425317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know which versions are best, in terms of defeqs</p>",
        "id": 586108380,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776425334
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you could also just write <code>Fin.mk k ⋯</code></p>",
        "id": 586113858,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1776427242
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Exactly. So I want to know from combinatorialists which one they prefer.</p>\n<p>My problem is not that I'm worried there is no solution. Rather that there are too many.</p>",
        "id": 586115273,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776427646
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This should be <code>ZMod (n + 1)</code>. The point is that an initial segment of naturals is the same as an initial segment of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Z/n\\Z</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span></span></span></span> for some big <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> from the point of view of eg arithmetic progressions of length 3</p>",
        "id": 586182384,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1776446509
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sounds good to me, but note that <code>ZMod n</code> doesn't come with an ordering.</p>",
        "id": 586182930,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776446720
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's (or should be made to be) a cyclic order, which would be enough to make sense of the initial segment</p>",
        "id": 586185588,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1776447674
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My instinct was also ZMod, but I didn't propose that because we don't yet have intervals or initial segments in cyclic orders, and also not much api for cyclic orders which would make this nice to use. I think the practical solution here would be to pick one of the approaches (eg, mine <span aria-label=\"stuck out tongue closed eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f61d\" role=\"img\" title=\"stuck out tongue closed eyes\">:stuck_out_tongue_closed_eyes:</span> ) with a comment to add the ZMod version once the api for cyclic preorders is improved</p>",
        "id": 586223477,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1776465820
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What's a cyclic order?</p>",
        "id": 586259576,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776501191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CircularOrder#doc\">docs#CircularOrder</a></p>",
        "id": 586260478,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1776502288
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- **No wrap-around principle**.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">A set of elements of `ℕ` is `m`-Freiman isomorphic to its image in `ZMod (n + 1)`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">if all elements of the set are at most `k` and `m * k ≤ n`, i.e. there is no wrap-around. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isAddFreimanIso_image_cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hkmn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsAddFreimanIso</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">bijOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">suffices</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InjOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MapsTo</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SurjOn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">CharP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natCast_injOn_Iio</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mono</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lt_succ_iff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le_mul_of_pos_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">bot_lt</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hkmn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">map_sum_eq_map_sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hsS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">htS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">castRingHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Multiset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">huk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hu</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sum_le_card_nsmul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">huk</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">CharP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natCast_injOn_Iio</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">congr_arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">all_goals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 586266776,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1776509391
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've PRd this in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38205\">#38205</a></p>\n<p>It reduces the technical debt, but doesn't get rid of it completely.</p>",
